       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults under physician supervision. The OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common regimen for inflammatory conditions\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided differently\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
